WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.089 --> 00:00:07.050
I don't wanna ride back with you
guys. Rather go shake this off.

2
00:00:07.717 --> 00:00:09.386
Yeah. sure. No. of course.

3
00:00:10.095 --> 00:00:13.598
Hey. Hey. hey. Just... Be
careful out there. all right?

4
00:00:15.475 --> 00:00:17.435
Yeah? Okay. And don't forget.

5
00:00:18.019 --> 00:00:22.107
tomorrow it's your turn for coffee
at the game film. all right?

6
00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.400
- Yeah.
- Bright and early.

7
00:00:27.153 --> 00:00:28.989
Hey. Coach. Bird by bird.

8
00:00:30.907 --> 00:00:32.366
Not that kind of bird.

9
00:00:37.622 --> 00:00:43.670
Blue moon You saw
me standing alone

10
00:00:44.212 --> 00:00:48.842
Without a dream in my heart

11
00:00:49.342 --> 00:00:52.053
Without a love of my own

12
00:00:56.892 --> 00:00:59.227
Mind the gap.

13
00:00:59.895 --> 00:01:03.315
This is the southbound
metropolitan line train to Aldgate.

14
00:01:07.694 --> 00:01:10.238
Doors closing. Stand clear
of the doors. please.

15
00:02:36.616 --> 00:02:38.535
It was moment after
moment like this.

16
00:02:38.618 --> 00:02:40.745
A real David versus
Goliath match.

17
00:02:41.288 --> 00:02:44.708
but where Goliath just curb-stomped
David in the back of the skull

18
00:02:44.791 --> 00:02:46.459
like in that Ed Norton movie.

19
00:02:46.918 --> 00:02:48.003
Moonrise Kingdom?

20
00:02:48.503 --> 00:02:49.588
I think that's it. yeah.

21
00:02:49.671 --> 00:02:53.091
Yeah. Well. for me. the match
was a real Cinderella story.

22
00:02:53.633 --> 00:02:57.053
If her glass slipper broke and
sliced her Achilles tendon.

23
00:02:57.137 --> 00:02:59.681
Thierry. was this just an
off day for the players?

24
00:02:59.764 --> 00:03:01.600
Or do we lay the blame
on the coaching staff?

25
00:03:01.683 --> 00:03:03.768
100% coaching staff.

26
00:03:03.852 --> 00:03:05.478
Those are good footballers.

27
00:03:06.104 --> 00:03:08.523
It just felt like
Richmond had no plan.

28
00:03:08.607 --> 00:03:12.110
- And what about Coach Beard?
- What about him. indeed.

29
00:03:12.193 --> 00:03:15.113
Coach Beard knew an aggressive
offensive strategy was a mistake.

30
00:03:15.196 --> 00:03:18.950
He should not have let Ted. Nathan
and Roy convince him otherwise.

31
00:03:19.034 --> 00:03:22.454
Great point. Thierry. Coach
Beard is Ted Lasso's number two.

32
00:03:22.537 --> 00:03:25.290
He's supposed to challenge him.
not just be a sniveling lackey.

33
00:03:26.291 --> 00:03:29.169
Look. Gary. the man
has no va-va-voom.

34
00:03:29.252 --> 00:03:34.216
Does anything say "sad. single man"
more than a chessboard coffee table?

35
00:03:36.051 --> 00:03:38.637
I know I'm French and expected
to say things like this.

36
00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.848
but I hate Coach Beard.

37
00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:45.143
Shut up. Thierry Henry.

38
00:03:45.227 --> 00:03:47.562
After Richard Montlaur
earned himself a red card.

39
00:03:47.646 --> 00:03:49.356
things went from bad to worse.

40
00:04:13.421 --> 00:04:14.422
Ted joining you?

41
00:04:14.506 --> 00:04:15.549
No.

42
00:04:15.632 --> 00:04:18.134
- Jane coming?
- We broke up.

43
00:04:18.218 --> 00:04:19.636
Shocking.

44
00:04:19.719 --> 00:04:21.763
She accused me of
being jealous. Me.

45
00:04:22.556 --> 00:04:24.766
Because I told her it's
hard to know where I stand.

46
00:04:24.849 --> 00:04:27.310
which it is. because she
never says "I love you."

47
00:04:27.394 --> 00:04:29.646
- Did you say it to her?
- I did.

48
00:04:29.729 --> 00:04:31.898
- And she didn't say it back.
- She did not.

49
00:04:33.316 --> 00:04:35.026
Thank you for helping
me relive that.

50
00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:37.862
Well. you must feel awful.

51
00:04:38.905 --> 00:04:41.700
Reason is powerless in
the expression of love.

52
00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.369
Nuh-uh. I meant about the match.

53
00:04:44.452 --> 00:04:47.455
What the hell was your
thinking behind those tactics?

54
00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:50.417
- Mae.
- All right. Enjoy your beer.

55
00:04:54.212 --> 00:04:55.589
But come on.

56
00:04:55.672 --> 00:04:58.717
There's no way you thought coming
out on the attack was a good idea.

57
00:04:59.384 --> 00:05:02.596
You basically left Zoreaux back
there to defend by himself.

58
00:05:04.681 --> 00:05:05.974
In a semifinal…

59
00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.102
A semifinal!

60
00:05:39.257 --> 00:05:41.468
Oi. Beard. Dropped your keys.

61
00:05:42.427 --> 00:05:43.428
Thanks.

62
00:05:43.511 --> 00:05:46.014
- Rough match. mate.
- We thought you needed a hug.

63
00:05:47.182 --> 00:05:49.768
- I thought you needed a hug.
- Do you wanna talk about it?

64
00:05:49.851 --> 00:05:51.394
We can talk and drink

65
00:05:51.478 --> 00:05:54.314
as long as we talk about
anything but the game and drink.

66
00:05:59.152 --> 00:06:01.714
- Have you ever been to Vegas?
- What's Ted like behind closed doors?

67
00:06:01.738 --> 00:06:03.823
How do you cope knowing
the universe is infinite

68
00:06:03.907 --> 00:06:06.034
but your consciousness
can end in a second?

69
00:06:11.915 --> 00:06:13.416
I've been to Vegas many times.

70
00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.920
One night is good. two nights
is perfect. three is too many.

71
00:06:17.003 --> 00:06:19.297
Ted is a man. Just a man.

72
00:06:19.798 --> 00:06:23.593
And as for the fragility of life.
I'm so glad someone finally asked.

73
00:06:23.677 --> 00:06:26.471
Because. yeah. I
got a few thoughts.

74
00:06:31.643 --> 00:06:35.272
And so. in conclusion.

75
00:06:35.355 --> 00:06:37.732
if this is all
indeed a simulation.

76
00:06:37.816 --> 00:06:40.694
which everything in my
experience suggests that it is.

77
00:06:41.194 --> 00:06:45.657
then all we can do is tip our caps
to the rascal pulling the strings.

78
00:06:47.617 --> 00:06:49.619
That's it. people.

79
00:06:49.703 --> 00:06:53.999
Just like my legs after a date
with a guy who kept correcting me.

80
00:06:54.082 --> 00:06:55.083
we're closed.

81
00:06:55.166 --> 00:06:56.960
You went on a date with Richard?

82
00:06:57.752 --> 00:07:00.589
I think you'll find.
Mae. it was two dates.

83
00:07:00.672 --> 00:07:01.673
Out.

84
00:07:02.507 --> 00:07:04.050
Coffee was a date.

85
00:07:20.442 --> 00:07:21.735
Where to next?

86
00:07:21.818 --> 00:07:24.988
Bed. This is England.
mate. Pubs shut at 11:30.

87
00:07:25.071 --> 00:07:28.116
Well. I'm not ready for the
night to end. Any ideas?

88
00:07:28.199 --> 00:07:30.327
What about Bones & Honey?

89
00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.786
As if.

90
00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:34.873
Private club. very swanky.
impossible to get in.

91
00:07:35.457 --> 00:07:38.209
Yeah. I heard they
once turned away Cher.

92
00:07:38.293 --> 00:07:41.338
Would you believe
They did such a thing?

93
00:07:41.421 --> 00:07:42.923
Well…

94
00:07:44.507 --> 00:07:48.053
Why don't we just head over
there and see what happens?

95
00:07:49.804 --> 00:07:51.097
I think there's a dress code.

96
00:08:00.899 --> 00:08:02.609
Mae. I love you!

97
00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.250
Taxi!

98
00:08:26.299 --> 00:08:27.968
- Welcome back. darling.
- Thank you.

99
00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:31.888
Good evening.

100
00:08:33.181 --> 00:08:34.724
Do we know each other?

101
00:08:34.808 --> 00:08:38.101
I don't think we do. sir. May
I see your membership card?

102
00:08:38.979 --> 00:08:41.356
University of Barcelona.
class of 2004?

103
00:08:41.438 --> 00:08:43.817
I went to Warwick. 2007.

104
00:08:44.484 --> 00:08:45.860
Sorry. you looked older.

105
00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:47.571
Are you a member here?

106
00:08:47.654 --> 00:08:49.990
Here? No. God. no. Never.

107
00:08:50.782 --> 00:08:54.661
Well. if you're not a member.
I'm afraid you can't come in.

108
00:08:54.744 --> 00:08:56.538
This is Bones & Honey.

109
00:08:57.664 --> 00:08:58.790
You are very rude.

110
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.167
What is your name?

111
00:09:01.251 --> 00:09:04.337
My name is Sarah Coombes.
What is your name?

112
00:09:04.421 --> 00:09:07.299
None of my business.

113
00:09:19.102 --> 00:09:20.604
Bones & Honey. may I help you?

114
00:09:21.688 --> 00:09:22.898
Do you mind?

115
00:09:24.649 --> 00:09:25.650
Speak.

116
00:09:25.734 --> 00:09:27.861
Hello. this is the fire brigade.

117
00:09:27.944 --> 00:09:31.656
It's very important that
we get in touch with...

118
00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:33.909
- Sarah Coombes.
- Sarah Coombes.

119
00:09:34.492 --> 00:09:35.744
That's you.

120
00:09:35.827 --> 00:09:38.663
Well. I'm very sorry. madam.
but your flat is on fire.

121
00:09:38.747 --> 00:09:40.916
You need to come down
here immediately.

122
00:09:42.792 --> 00:09:44.419
- Now what?
- Act cool.

123
00:09:47.631 --> 00:09:48.882
Orion's Belt!

124
00:09:51.468 --> 00:09:52.719
Amazing.

125
00:09:54.471 --> 00:09:56.640
We're walking. We're walking.

126
00:10:00.435 --> 00:10:01.478
You did it.

127
00:10:02.145 --> 00:10:04.022
You did what Cher couldn't do.

128
00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:07.108
I actually feel bad
for Sarah Coombes.

129
00:10:07.192 --> 00:10:08.985
Nah. Think how excited she'll be

130
00:10:09.069 --> 00:10:11.988
when she realizes that her
place didn't actually burn down.

131
00:10:12.072 --> 00:10:14.783
Tomorrow will be the most beautiful
day of Sarah Coombes's life.

132
00:10:15.575 --> 00:10:17.410
Her apartment will look
more amazing to her

133
00:10:17.494 --> 00:10:19.579
than any place any of
us have ever lived.

134
00:10:21.456 --> 00:10:22.457
Here we go.

135
00:10:25.627 --> 00:10:27.379
Okay. gentlemen. plan of attack.

136
00:10:30.715 --> 00:10:32.050
What's wrong?

137
00:10:35.512 --> 00:10:37.055
I don't think we belong here.

138
00:10:37.764 --> 00:10:39.307
Knock that shit off.

139
00:10:39.975 --> 00:10:40.976
We belong.

140
00:10:42.185 --> 00:10:44.185
If you could be anywhere.
where would you wanna be?

141
00:10:44.771 --> 00:10:45.855
Here. right?

142
00:10:47.148 --> 00:10:48.525
Then act like it.

143
00:10:50.694 --> 00:10:52.320
Now who wants an
overpriced beer?

144
00:10:54.573 --> 00:10:56.533
Who wants an overpriced
beer that I'm paying for?

145
00:10:58.618 --> 00:10:59.911
Find us a spot.

146
00:10:59.995 --> 00:11:02.706
And feel free to strut.

147
00:11:28.106 --> 00:11:29.316
What can I get you. sir?

148
00:11:30.191 --> 00:11:33.194
- Four beers. please.
- Would you like them in glass. sir?

149
00:11:33.278 --> 00:11:34.571
No.

150
00:11:49.044 --> 00:11:51.630
Relax. fella. It's just angles.

151
00:11:51.713 --> 00:11:53.882
Maybe if you'd paid attention
in trig. you'd do better.

152
00:11:55.592 --> 00:11:58.845
Shall we have a friendly
wager on this shot?

153
00:11:59.429 --> 00:12:00.931
Say. 20 quid?

154
00:12:01.014 --> 00:12:02.015
Hold on.

155
00:12:02.599 --> 00:12:03.975
What's trig?

156
00:12:07.187 --> 00:12:08.271
Trigonometry.

157
00:12:08.355 --> 00:12:09.981
Maths. Yeah?

158
00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:11.775
- Yeah. Yeah.
- Yeah.

159
00:12:11.858 --> 00:12:13.860
Sorry. but where
did you guys study?

160
00:12:15.195 --> 00:12:18.240
There you are. lads. Ha.
Thought I'd lost you.

161
00:12:18.323 --> 00:12:21.284
Then where would I
be? Sad and alone.

162
00:12:22.118 --> 00:12:23.203
Evening. gents.

163
00:12:23.286 --> 00:12:25.372
I see you've met my protégés.

164
00:12:25.455 --> 00:12:27.582
I'm Professor Declan
Patrick Aloysius MacManus.

165
00:12:27.666 --> 00:12:29.918
At your service. I assure
you. the pleasure is mine.

166
00:12:30.001 --> 00:12:35.382
But. I must tell you. these lads here were
the best of the best at Oxford itself.

167
00:12:36.466 --> 00:12:39.511
And now. we're just having a
wee liquid reunion. aren't we?

168
00:12:40.554 --> 00:12:42.847
- Oxford?
- Yeah. what were you professor of?

169
00:12:42.931 --> 00:12:45.392
Economics and management.
till I retired.

170
00:12:45.475 --> 00:12:47.269
At Oxford.

171
00:12:47.852 --> 00:12:48.853
That is correct.

172
00:12:49.479 --> 00:12:50.730
We were at Oxford.

173
00:12:52.774 --> 00:12:53.775
Christ Church.

174
00:12:55.068 --> 00:12:56.570
Which college were you?

175
00:12:58.780 --> 00:12:59.906
Christ Church?

176
00:13:01.116 --> 00:13:02.284
Our main rivals.

177
00:13:03.535 --> 00:13:05.328
I'm a Merton man. myself.

178
00:13:05.412 --> 00:13:07.038
Merton.

179
00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:09.749
Where'd you live?

180
00:13:09.833 --> 00:13:11.793
Right across from the chapel.

181
00:13:12.586 --> 00:13:16.006
Nothing like waking up every morning to
the sound of the Dobson Organ at 8:15.

182
00:13:16.089 --> 00:13:17.257
am I right?

183
00:13:20.969 --> 00:13:23.263
You Merton motherfucker.

184
00:13:25.807 --> 00:13:28.727
How are you. sir?
When did you leave?

185
00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:31.479
2015. The year we beat
Cambridge in the boat race

186
00:13:31.563 --> 00:13:33.982
by six and a half
lengths. lest we forget.

187
00:13:34.065 --> 00:13:36.568
I was on that crew.
I was the cox.

188
00:13:36.651 --> 00:13:38.695
Yes. you were. you bastard.

189
00:13:40.822 --> 00:13:43.783
Harry Gill is here!
Harry Gill. in this pub!

190
00:13:43.867 --> 00:13:45.243
Hey!

191
00:13:46.119 --> 00:13:47.621
Marvelous. Marvelous.

192
00:13:48.496 --> 00:13:50.040
Professor McGonagall
taught us a lot.

193
00:13:50.916 --> 00:13:53.793
But the main thing he taught
us was the value of money.

194
00:13:54.836 --> 00:13:56.838
£20. You're on.

195
00:14:03.178 --> 00:14:04.971
I got it. I got it.

196
00:14:05.055 --> 00:14:06.306
I've got five.

197
00:14:08.016 --> 00:14:09.017
Save one for a kebab.

198
00:14:10.227 --> 00:14:11.811
Eccentric geniuses.

199
00:14:11.895 --> 00:14:13.021
Right.

200
00:14:13.104 --> 00:14:17.817
17. 18. 19. 20.

201
00:14:17.901 --> 00:14:19.569
How's that for trigonometry?

202
00:14:21.112 --> 00:14:22.322
We got there.

203
00:14:37.212 --> 00:14:38.213
Yes!

204
00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:43.134
- Fair play!
- Good on you.

205
00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.221
Next round is on us.

206
00:14:46.304 --> 00:14:47.514
Anything you like.

207
00:14:47.597 --> 00:14:50.100
- Three big boots of ale?
- This guy.

208
00:14:52.852 --> 00:14:56.189
Oi. How'd you know all
that stuff about Oxford?

209
00:14:57.357 --> 00:15:00.569
I dated a professor at Oxford.
And I listen more than I talk.

210
00:15:03.238 --> 00:15:04.573
I'll be right back.

211
00:15:06.408 --> 00:15:07.826
Oi.

212
00:15:07.909 --> 00:15:09.869
What a legend you are!

213
00:15:57.709 --> 00:15:59.628
Hard to forget a game like that.

214
00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:03.548
You know what will help? Going
to see the woman you love.

215
00:16:04.591 --> 00:16:06.259
Exactly. But it's clear to me

216
00:16:06.343 --> 00:16:09.054
that Coach Beard doesn't
think he's worthy of Jane.

217
00:16:09.137 --> 00:16:10.388
I know.

218
00:16:10.472 --> 00:16:14.893
Beard's self-esteem is so low. he
will need a pep talk to kill himself.

219
00:16:14.976 --> 00:16:17.729
and I would like to
give that pep talk.

220
00:16:17.812 --> 00:16:19.314
Shut up. Thierry Henry.

221
00:16:22.067 --> 00:16:24.110
Goddamn fucking shit!

222
00:16:25.946 --> 00:16:27.113
Is there a problem here?

223
00:16:27.197 --> 00:16:30.325
Yeah. This nail on your faux
Persian flea market coffee table

224
00:16:30.408 --> 00:16:31.534
just tore my pants.

225
00:16:31.618 --> 00:16:33.703
Sir. can I see your
membership card. please?

226
00:16:38.708 --> 00:16:39.876
My friends are in there.

227
00:16:42.379 --> 00:16:43.380
Goddamn it.

228
00:16:45.632 --> 00:16:48.218
I'm sure you know that
your trousers are ripped.

229
00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:53.390
They're designed that way.

230
00:16:54.641 --> 00:16:56.643
To make it easier for
people to kiss my ass.

231
00:16:58.603 --> 00:17:01.481
Be careful. We have
decency laws in England.

232
00:17:01.565 --> 00:17:02.691
You'll get arrested.

233
00:17:02.774 --> 00:17:05.151
I wasn't aware the laws
were so restrictive here.

234
00:17:05.901 --> 00:17:08.530
Oh. yeah. We're a
repressed nation.

235
00:17:09.237 --> 00:17:12.699
One exposed arse can bring
down the monarchy itself.

236
00:17:13.785 --> 00:17:15.910
How dare you speak of
Prince Andrew that way.

237
00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:18.247
I could fix those for you.

238
00:17:20.083 --> 00:17:21.251
I live over there.

239
00:17:22.458 --> 00:17:23.879
In that pointy building?

240
00:17:24.838 --> 00:17:25.839
No.

241
00:17:49.404 --> 00:17:50.614
Take your trousers off.

242
00:17:52.032 --> 00:17:53.241
You're not in charge of me.

243
00:18:01.207 --> 00:18:03.376
I'll give you something
to wear in the meantime.

244
00:18:13.845 --> 00:18:15.722
People come and go from my life.

245
00:18:16.556 --> 00:18:18.850
I've always kept a
pair of their trousers.

246
00:18:20.977 --> 00:18:22.812
This rack is like my memoirs.

247
00:18:25.565 --> 00:18:26.566
These should fit.

248
00:18:27.776 --> 00:18:29.110
Whose were these?

249
00:18:29.194 --> 00:18:30.445
An old lover.

250
00:18:30.528 --> 00:18:31.738
Where's he now?

251
00:18:31.821 --> 00:18:32.864
Dead.

252
00:18:35.408 --> 00:18:36.618
You dropped your keys.

253
00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.211
You ever look back on a relationship
and regret it had ended?

254
00:18:47.379 --> 00:18:48.463
Been doing it all day.

255
00:18:49.464 --> 00:18:51.758
I've loved every man in my life.

256
